    "subject": "legal-medicine",
    "originalNumber": 523,
    "stem": "A 57-year-old man is brought to the physician by his\nwife because his skin has appeared yellow for 3 weeks.\nExamination shows jaundice and scleral icterus. His\ntotal serum bilirubin level is 8 mg/dL with a direct\ncomponent of 6.2 mg/dL. A CT scan of the abdomen\nshows a large lesion in the head of the pancreas. When\nthe results are initially discussed, the patient says that\nhe does not want to hear the report, and his wife agrees\nto abide by his wishes. Which of the following is the\nmost appropriate course of action?",
